CREATE INDEX products_search_idx ON products USING GIN (search_vector);
```

New route in `routes/products.js`, parameterized (never string-concatenate `req.query.q` into SQL):

```js
router.get("/search", async (req, res) => {
  const q = (req.query.q || "").trim();
  if (!q) return res.json([]);
  const rows = await db.query(
    `SELECT id, sku, name, price_cents,
            ts_rank(search_vector, websearch_to_tsquery('english', $1)) AS rank
     FROM products
     WHERE active AND search_vector @@ websearch_to_tsquery('english', $1)
     ORDER BY rank DESC
     LIMIT 50`,
    [q]
  );
  res.json(rows);
});
```

`websearch_to_tsquery` over `plainto_tsquery` because it handles multi-word natural queries (and quoted phrases) the way users actually type them.

Left out: typo tolerance (would need `pg_trgm` + trigram index alongside this if that matters), and tuning the A/B weight split once you see real query patterns.
